      "message": "So it\u0027s an interesting discussion around what belongs in the ec/zephyr/boards/... configurations as opposed to what appears in ec/zephyr/Kconfig* files.\nLooking forward, I guess the idea is that what is in the boards/ configuration will map roughly to standard configs in zephyr, so I can see that defining the stack sizes for standard tasks like main, idle, workqueue etc. in this config is OK, and have the EC task defaults in ec/zephyr/Kconfig*.\nI actually don\u0027t think the EC task stack sizes like PD, USB_CHG belong here.\nEspecially as new tasks are optionally added, it would be better to have these in a specifically EC location.\nIt would also be cleaner to have separate Kconfig.stacks for each EC CPU type e.g Kconfig.stacks_npcx9 or something like that. Maybe.\nIt\u0027s not obvious to me what the best organisation is, so OK to keep it like this until it gets cleaned up futher.",
